title op6: a delta whose lost names straddle the split

# The residual conflict the settlement keeps DELIBERATELY, with the
# impossibility on the record as the reason it is correct rather than
# provisional.
#
# Onto un-shares z into its own dnode.  Off-of renames x to aa and z
# to cc, so the delta is lost {x, z} gained {aa, cc} -- and the two
# lost names now sit in DIFFERENT fragments of onto's split.
#
# The gains cannot be partitioned to follow.  Content and position
# evidence cannot say whether aa succeeds x or z, and the document's
# impossibility argument stands: nothing observable distinguishes the
# labels.  So this conflicts, and it should.
#
# The verdict is the same before and after the settlement, and so is
# the gold.  What changes is the REASON and the report.  Today the
# engine says it could not pair two renames.  Under set-valued
# succession it says a group lost {x, z} and gained {aa, cc} across a
# split -- a true statement about what happened rather than a
# statement about what the algorithm could not do.
#
# THAT DISTINCTION IS INVISIBLE TO THIS SUITE, and saying so is half
# the reason the fixture exists.  The gold tier checks the decided
# tree and the conflict kinds; it does not read the report's wording.
# So no fixture can tell the old reason from the new one.  That
# matters more than it sounds, because "at least it fails loudly" was
# the defence of the old behaviour, and loudness lives entirely in
# text this tier cannot see.  Proving the report improved needs a
# census-tier or manifest assertion, and that is owed work, not
# covered work.
#
# WORKED OUTCOME (by hand, before any implementation ran)
#   believed moves:  none; no directory changed
#   deltas:          pool 10 lost {x, z}, gained {aa, cc}; the lost
#                    set straddles onto's fragments 10-100 and 30-200
#   decisions:       none for the region.  It is quarantined and
#                    falls back to onto: x and y on 10-100, z on
#                    30-200
#   conflicts:       one, kind pooling
#   emission:        nothing; a quarantined region emits no edits
#
# CONFIDENCE.  The conflict KIND and the quarantine set are the least
# certain lines here.  Both are taken by analogy with the
# two-renames/ arm of 6-ambiguous-succession.tree, which is the same
# straddling shape inside a larger fixture and which the engine has
# actually run, rather than reasoned from the rules directly.  If the
# engine reports differently, read that fixture before assuming this
# one is wrong.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      10-100: z

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared/
      10-100: aa = v0
      10-100: cc
      10-100: y

# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect conflict pooling
expect quarantined /shared/x
expect quarantined /shared/y
expect quarantined /shared/z

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: shared
      10-100: x = v0
      10-100: y
      30-200: z = v0
